{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 35, :comments ["<b>Glory</b> — HaShem will bequeath them glory of wealth and riches, but fools — disgrace will be raised upon them. The meaning: that they will cause people to despise them." "<b>Lift up disgrace</b> — concerning every man he speaks, like: וצדיקים ככפיר יבטח (and the righteous are bold as a lion). Another interpretation: a fool lifts up and honors a man." "<b>Disgrace</b> — like בא זדון (outrage comes), missing [the word] 'man.'"], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:20:59.311253292Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}